
# 📘 **BEGINNER CHEAT-SHEET — UNITY MOVEMENT & ROTATION (DAY 1 NOTES)**



# 🟦 **SECTION 1 — MOVEMENT METHODS (GAMEOBJECT)**
| Method                       | Description                     | Parameters                          | Example                                                                                               |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **transform.position**       | Sets/gets exact world position  | `Vector3(x, y, z)`                  | `transform.position = new Vector3(0, 1, 0);`                                                          |
| **transform.Translate()**    | Moves object by an amount       | `(x, y, z)` in local OR world space | `transform.Translate(0, 0, 1 * Time.deltaTime);`                                                      |
| **Vector3.MoveTowards()**    | Moves from A → B at fixed speed | `(current, target, speed)`          | `transform.position = Vector3.MoveTowards(transform.position, target.position, 5f * Time.deltaTime);` |
| **Vector3.Lerp()**           | Smooth gradual movement         | `(from, to, t)` where t = 0–1       | `transform.position = Vector3.Lerp(transform.position, targetPos, 0.1f);`                             |
| **Vector3.Slerp()**          | Smooth movement on curved path  | `(from, to, t)`                     | `transform.position = Vector3.Slerp(p1, p2, 0.1f);`                                                   |
| **Rigidbody.MovePosition()** | Physics-friendly movement       | `targetPosition`                    | `rb.MovePosition(transform.position + transform.forward * speed * Time.fixedDeltaTime);`              |

